---
import LayoutRedesign from '../../layouts/LayoutRedesign.astro';
import { SITE_URL, LINKEDIN, GITHUB } from '../../lib/site';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Nicolò Cabrelli',
  jobTitle: 'Full-stack developer',
  url: SITE_URL,
  sameAs: [GITHUB, LINKEDIN],
  address: {
    '@type': 'PostalAddress',
    addressLocality: 'Pontremoli',
    addressRegion: 'Tuscany',
    addressCountry: 'IT',
  },
};
---
<LayoutRedesign
  lang="en"
  title="Nicolò Cabrelli — Full-stack developer · Solo founder"
  description="I design, build and ship complete web products — from database to interface. Two SaaS platforms live, built solo. Available for freelance projects and remote roles."
  ogDescription="Complete web products, from database to interface. Two SaaS platforms live, built solo."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  alternates={[
    { hreflang: 'it', href: `${SITE_URL}/` },
    { hreflang: 'en', href: `${SITE_URL}/en/` },
  ]}
>
<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap top-inner">
    <a class="logo" href="/en/"><b>nc</b>.cabrelli</a>
    <nav class="main" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="#work">work</a>
      <a href="#method" class="hide-m">method</a>
      <a href="#profile" class="hide-m">profile</a>
      <a href="#contact">contact</a>
      <a class="lang" href="/" hreflang="it" aria-label="Passa all'italiano">it / <b>en</b></a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

<div class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">pontremoli, italy · available for remote work</p>
    <h1>I build <em>complete</em> web products. Solo.</h1>
    <p class="sub">I'm Nicolò Cabrelli, a self-taught full-stack developer and solo founder. I design the system, write the code, ship it to production and keep it running — from database to interface, from first commit to live domain.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-solid" href="mailto:nicolocabrelli@pm.me">Email me</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/tradingmindos" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicolocabrelli-tradingmindos" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-facts">
      <span><b>2</b> SaaS platforms in production</span>
      <span><b>end-to-end</b> — design → deploy</span>
      <span><b>it / en</b></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="work">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-label"><b>selected</b> work</p>

    <article class="dossier fade">
      <aside class="d-meta">
        <span class="status">live</span>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>role</dt><dd>everything — design, code, infra</dd></div>
          <div><dt>type</dt><dd>SaaS · trading psychology</dd></div>
          <div><dt>domain</dt><dd><a href="https://tradingmindos.com" rel="noopener">tradingmindos.com ↗</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
      <div class="d-body">
        <h3><a href="https://tradingmindos.com" rel="noopener">Trading Mind OS <span class="ext">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p class="lead">A platform that helps traders manage the hardest part of trading: their own mind. Designed and built from scratch, by one person.</p>
        <div class="schematic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 680 150" role="img" aria-label="Trading Mind OS architecture" class="reveal">
            <path class="wire" d="M150 45 H 210"/>
            <path class="wire" d="M370 45 H 430"/>
            <path class="wire hot" d="M290 68 V 118 H 430"/>
            <path class="wire" d="M150 118 H 210 M 330 118 H 400 V 45 H 430"/>
            <g class="node hot"><rect x="30" y="22" width="120" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="90" y="42" text-anchor="middle">React SPA</text><text x="90" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">widget dashboard</text></g>
            <g class="node"><rect x="210" y="22" width="160" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="290" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Supabase RPC</text><text x="290" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">server-enforced trial</text></g>
            <g class="node hot"><rect x="430" y="22" width="220" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="540" y="42" text-anchor="middle">PostgreSQL + RLS</text><text x="540" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">row-level security per user</text></g>
            <g class="node"><rect x="30" y="95" width="120" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="90" y="115" text-anchor="middle">MetaTrader 5</text><text x="90" y="131" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">custom EA</text></g>
            <g class="node"><rect x="210" y="95" width="120" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="270" y="115" text-anchor="middle">Bridge</text><text x="270" y="131" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">live trade sync</text></g>
            <g class="node"><rect x="430" y="95" width="220" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="540" y="115" text-anchor="middle">Anthropic API</text><text x="540" y="131" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">AI coach, server-side</text></g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="decisions">
          <div><span><b>Security enforced server-side</b>, not in the client: trials and permissions live in Postgres via RPC, with row-level security on every table.</span></div>
          <div><span><b>A custom MetaTrader 5 bridge</b> syncs real trades into the platform — no manual entry.</span></div>
          <div><span><b>Multi-currency</b> (USD / EUR / GBP) and a configurable dashboard with per-user layout persistence.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-tags">
          <span>react</span><span>vite</span><span>supabase</span><span>postgresql</span><span>cloudflare</span><span>anthropic api</span><span>metatrader 5</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="dossier fade">
      <aside class="d-meta">
        <span class="status">live</span>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>role</dt><dd>everything — platform and content</dd></div>
          <div><dt>type</dt><dd>education platform</dd></div>
          <div><dt>domain</dt><dd><a href="https://app.soravent.com" rel="noopener">app.soravent.com ↗</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
      <div class="d-body">
        <h3><a href="https://app.soravent.com" rel="noopener">SORAVENT <span class="ext">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p class="lead">A premium Italian-language trading education platform. From idea to launch-ready in one week of work: authentication, content modules, reading state, a structured journal, PDF generation, and a subscription flow.</p>
        <div class="schematic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 680 73" role="img" aria-label="SORAVENT architecture" class="reveal">
            <path class="wire" d="M150 45 H 190"/>
            <path class="wire" d="M330 45 H 370"/>
            <path class="wire hot" d="M510 45 H 550"/>
            <g class="node"><rect x="30" y="22" width="120" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="90" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Auth</text><text x="90" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">numbered-slot access</text></g>
            <g class="node hot"><rect x="190" y="22" width="140" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="260" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Content modules</text><text x="260" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">research + mind</text></g>
            <g class="node"><rect x="370" y="22" width="140" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="440" y="42" text-anchor="middle">Journal</text><text x="440" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">state + progress</text></g>
            <g class="node hot"><rect x="550" y="22" width="100" height="46" rx="4"/><text x="600" y="42" text-anchor="middle">PDF engine</text><text x="600" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">export</text></g>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="decisions">
          <div><span><b>A complete product, not a course on Notion</b>: reading state, a user passport, a founding offer with 50 numbered slots.</span></div>
          <div><span><b>Speed as proof</b>: built from scratch to launch-ready in days, not months.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-tags">
          <span>react</span><span>supabase</span><span>postgresql</span><span>cloudflare</span><span>pdf generation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="dossier fade">
      <aside class="d-meta">
        <span class="status">live</span>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>role</dt><dd>development, SEO, delivery</dd></div>
          <div><dt>type</dt><dd>client work</dd></div>
          <div><dt>domain</dt><dd><a href="https://taxi-pontremoli.com" rel="noopener">taxi-pontremoli.com ↗</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
      <div class="d-body">
        <h3><a href="https://taxi-pontremoli.com" rel="noopener">Taxi Pontremoli <span class="ext">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p class="lead">A production website for a local business, delivered end-to-end: fast, optimized for Google, deployed on the edge. Today it brings ride requests straight from search.</p>
        <div class="decisions">
          <div><span><b>Technical SEO + Google Business Profile</b>: the site doesn't exist to exist — it exists to be found.</span></div>
          <div><span>"Simple, clear and thorough. I've already seen results — and my customers love it too." — <b>Michele, owner</b></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stack-tags">
          <span>astro</span><span>tailwind</span><span>cloudflare pages</span><span>technical seo</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section id="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-label"><b>method</b> — how I work</p>
    <div class="method fade">
      <article>
        <h4>Product <span>design → ship</span></h4>
        <p>I start from the problem, not the stack. I design the system, define the smallest scope that creates value, and put it online. One product in production beats ten prototypes.</p>
        <p class="tools">design in code · iteration on real users</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h4>Engineering <span>frontend + backend</span></h4>
        <p>React and Astro on the interface, Postgres and Supabase on the data, with row-level security and server-enforced logic. I integrate external APIs where they earn their place — AI included.</p>
        <p class="tools">react · vite · astro · supabase · postgresql · node · rest api · anthropic api</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h4>Operations <span>deploy → maintain</span></h4>
        <p>Cloudflare deploys, DNS, security, analytics, technical SEO. Launch isn't the finish line: I verify in production, measure, and fix.</p>
        <p class="tools">cloudflare pages · git · 2fa everywhere · web analytics</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="profile">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sec-label"><b>profile</b></p>
    <div class="profile fade">
      <div class="txt">
        <p><b>Self-taught by necessity, systematic by choice.</b> I learned to code by building real products, with real users and real problems — not by following tutorials. Every project on this page went through my hands in every part: database schema, interface, security, deploy, domain.</p>
        <p>I live in Pontremoli, in Lunigiana, Tuscany, and I work remotely. This place taught me something I carry into code: things built well last, and the person who built them answers for them. If you need a change a year from now, you know who to call.</p>
        <p>I'm open to <b>freelance projects and remote full-stack roles</b>.</p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <img src="/nico.webp" alt="Nicolò Cabrelli" width="240" height="240" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>pontremoli, lunigiana — 44.37° n, 9.88° e</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="contact" class="contact">
  <div class="wrap fade">
    <p class="sec-label"><b>contact</b></p>
    <h2>Have a system to build? <em>Let's talk.</em></h2>
    <a class="mail" href="mailto:nicolocabrelli@pm.me">nicolocabrelli@pm.me</a>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://github.com/tradingmindos" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicolocabrelli-tradingmindos" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap foot">
    <span>© 2026 Nicolò Cabrelli · C.F. 90021180451</span>
    <a href="/lunigiana">Websites for local businesses in Lunigiana →</a>
  </div>
</footer>
</LayoutRedesign>
